title: "vxvhal: an Eclipse Kuksa provider serving Android Automotive's gRPC Vehicle HAL from VSS signals"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Djaafri"
    given-names: "Fouzi"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-7173-9344"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vxedge/vxvhal"
url: "https://vxedge.dev"
version: "0.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - android-automotive
  - vehicle-hal
  - vss
  - eclipse-kuksa
  - software-defined-vehicle
  - testbed
abstract: >-
  vxvhal serves Android Automotive's gRPC Vehicle HAL (GRPCVehicleHardware's VehicleServer) from
  COVESA VSS signals in an Eclipse Kuksa databroker, through a mapping of VSS path to AAOS property
  and unit. It gives an AAOS guest in a vxedge virtual prototype trial a production-shaped vehicle
  data path. It is not a vendor Vehicle HAL.
